#N canvas 20 20 1400 1200 12;
#X text 20 20 e_delay -- one drum track's delay \, in c_kit beside its c_voice: echoes of the track a note value apart \, 1/2 to 1/32 \, straight \, triplet or dotted \, which follow the tempo \, with feedback and a level (Brendan \, 2026-11-05). ref/module/sequencer.md, f 70;
#X text 20 130 creation arg 1: c_kit's \$0 \, for the length of a step and the throws \, arg 2: its pad \, 1 to 16. In: its voice's sound at the level \, thrown by c_voice to \$1-d\$2. inlet: delay-time <steps> \, a sixteenth a step \, feedback <0-100> \, delay <0-100> \, the level \, and send <0-100> \, its track's send to the reverb \, from c_steps through c_kit. Out: the echoes \, thrown to c_kit's \$1-out \, and at the send to e_verb's \$1-verb., f 70;
#X obj 20 300 catch~ \$1-d\$2;
#X obj 700 300 inlet;
#X obj 700 340 route delay-time feedback delay send;
#X obj 20 440 +~;
#X obj 20 480 delwrite~ \$0-buf 4000;
#X obj 300 400 line~;
#X obj 300 440 delread4~ \$0-buf;
#X obj 460 480 *~ 0;
#X obj 300 640 throw~ \$1-out;
#X obj 500 600 *~ 0;
#X obj 500 640 throw~ \$1-verb;
#X obj 120 540 env~ 4096 2048;
#X obj 120 580 < 20;
#X obj 120 620 change;
#X obj 120 660 sel 1 0;
#X msg 220 700 stop;
#X obj 120 760 del 350;
#X obj 120 800 f;
#X obj 120 840 sel 0;
#X obj 120 880 t b b;
#X msg 120 920 0;
#X msg 220 920 clear;
#X obj 700 420 > 0;
#X obj 700 460 t f f;
#X obj 700 500 sel 1 0;
#X obj 700 540 t b b;
#X msg 700 580 1;
#X obj 700 960 switch~;
#X obj 900 420 expr \$f1 / 100 * 0.95;
#X obj 900 460 expr pow(\$f1 / 100 \, 2);
#X obj 1100 420 f 2;
#X obj 1100 460 * 125;
#X obj 1100 500 clip 3 3990;
#X obj 1100 620 - 1.45125;
#X obj 1100 540 t f f;
#X msg 1100 660 \$1 50;
#X obj 1200 580 + 100;
#X obj 1200 340 r \$1-step;
#X obj 1200 380 t b f;
#X text 700 680 The time is its steps times a step's length \, which c_kit works out from the tempo bus \, so the echoes follow the tempo \, gliding there over 50 ms. The buffer holds 4 s: a dotted half \, twelve steps \, at 45 BPM or faster. The feedback tops out at 0.95 \, which never runs away \, and the send is squared \, as the level is in c_voice. The level is what goes into the delay \, so echoes already made ring out when it goes down. c_voice's throw reaches the catch~ a block late \, 64 samples \, 1.45 ms at 44.1 kHz \, since c_kit runs the delays before the voices \, so the read is that much shorter and an echo lands on its note value., f 50;
#X text 20 1000 switch~: on while the level is above 0 \, and at 0 \, off once what goes into the delay has been below -80 dBFS for a delay's time and 100 ms: then every echo left in it has been heard \, and the buffer is cleared \, so a longer time later finds nothing old in it. A switch~ starts off. While it is off its voice throws it nothing but zeros \, since the level is 0 \, so the catch~ never fills up., f 60;
